## Errors & Mistakes
I over-cut on the first pass. engineering.md was 29 lines and reduced the
entire subtraction stance to three sentences. Aaron caught it. Root cause: I
followed an adversarial "still-too-much" critic agent that scored every
sentence against "would a competent model do the wrong thing without this."
That test deletes deliberate personal stance, because a competent model does
something merely acceptable instead of what Aaron wants. Restored in a second
pass.

Second mistake, caught by a critic: "Say no by default" has no addressee. In a
session the only party to say no to is the user, and the harness prompt
requires delivering the requested scope. The Do less section now opens with
"This governs what you propose, not what you are asked for," which is
load-bearing. Do not reorder it away from the top.

Third: I wrote "Give a requirement more scrutiny when it comes from someone
senior or respected." In an agent session the user IS the senior requester, so
that line aimed maximum suspicion at Aaron's own instructions. Deleted.

