## Hints for Future Agents
The adjudicator pattern is what made the critique usable. Four critics
produced 40+ findings; the adjudicator rejected 7 of 10 serious ones as
misquotes, because those critics had read the file before a revision landed.
Always adjudicate against the CURRENT file before acting on critic output.

Adversarial critic agents reliably over-cut prompt artifacts. Weight Aaron's
stated preference above their scoring. See memory
compression-loses-substance.

## Codebase Discoveries
~/.claude/rules/*.md auto-loads into every session INDEPENDENTLY of
~/.claude/CLAUDE.md. Verified: CLAUDE_global.md had zero @import lines, yet
all seven rules files appeared in the session context. This is what made
deleting CLAUDE_global.md safe in a later commit.

Git history shows these rules were last tuned for Fable 5 (83a9a71, f0ef5f1).
That tuning was stale for Opus 5.

